              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mūrex, mūricis — \"the purple shellfish, murex; purple dye\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ex mūrice color purpureus fit. A purple colour is made from the murex shell."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, masculine: mūrex, mūricis m. Thousands of these sea snails went into a little purple dye. English keeps murex."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mūrex is usually traced to Greek myax 'sea mussel' (EtymDB); Lewis & Short give the sense but no source, so the path is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
